Common AC Problems
If your air conditioner is not working correctly, you may notice:
    • Warm air coming from vents 
    • Weak or uneven airflow 
    • Refrigerant leaks 
    • Frozen evaporator coils 
    • Faulty thermostats 
    • Strange noises or vibrations 
    • Water leaking around the unit 
    • Frequent cycling 
    • Higher energy bills 
Addressing these issues early helps prevent costly repairs and extends the life of your HVAC system.
